          </modifiers>
          <profiles>
            <profile name="Limpet Mine" id="df3a-aed2-fa57-750e" hidden="false" typeId="090c-b12e-592a-9874" typeName="Weapon">
              <characteristics>
                <characteristic name="Type" typeId="f90e-171a-4ca6-3845">GRENADE</characteristic>
                <characteristic name="Range" typeId="31a7-b5e8-41dc-5fd1">6&quot;</characteristic>
                <characteristic name="Keywords" typeId="8cd6-8018-f2da-5ede">BLAST 3&quot;, HEAVY, SCATTER, CONSUMABLE</characteristic>
                <characteristic name="Rules" typeId="87f0-637b-734a-22eb">Limpet mines may only be used once a battle. When you roll to attack with a Limpet Mine, note the location the mine lands with a marker or token.


Alternatively, you may attack with the Limpet Mine in melee, using your Ranged characteristic to hit. If the attack hits, the Mine is attached to the enemy model.


In either case, do not immediately roll for Injury. Instead, the mine detonates at the end of the turn, rolling for the injury with 3d6 (adding the dice together!) to any model under the center of the blast (i.e where the mine landed, or the model it was attached to), and rolling for an injury as normal for anyone else caught in the explosion.</characteristic>
              </characteristics>
            </profile>
          </profiles>
        </selectionEntry>
        <selectionEntry name="Chain Kura" id="ff14-6bda-4958-a507" hidden="true" import="true" type="upgrade">
